  "follow": "Follow Helios for the next AI launch, with the fine print read for you.",
  "caption": {
    "text": "Anthropic put Claude for Google Workspace into public beta on October 6, 2026, adding a Claude sidebar to Google Docs, Sheets and Slides on all paid Claude plans. Anthropic says it also released beta connectors that let Claude create and edit Google files from the Claude chat. (Public beta means a release open to all eligible users that Anthropic says still has known limits.)\n\nClaude can edit files directly. Anthropic says it asks for approval before changes by default and always pauses before adding a link or removing anyone's access. Its beta limits include no Firefox support and Google's six-minute cap on any single operation. Gemini is already built into these Google apps, and 9to5Google frames the add-on as useful for people already invested in Claude. The capability and security claims come from Anthropic, and the sources found no independent testing.\n\nWould you let an AI edit your shared documents without asking first?\n\nFollow Helios for AI launches with the fine print read for you.",
